  "severity": "important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-94300:\n\tReplaying GSS-TSIG signed UDP messages can result in memory corruption in named. An attacker who can capture a previously signed UDP message can replay it while the negotiated TSIG key is still valid. By also sending crafted queries to a zone the attacker controls, the attacker may potentially achieve remote code execution.\n\nCVE-2026-19630:\n\tInbound-message resource exhaustion (CWE-400) leading to denial of service. No configuration precondition; version applicability is the deciding factor. Affected versions: 9.11.0-9.18.50, 9.20.0-9.20.29, 9.21.0-9.21.26.\n",
